  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You receive a string `s` consisting only of the characters `'0'` and `'1'`. In one operation, you can change any `'0'` to `'1'` or vice versa.\n\nThe string is called alternating if no two adjacent characters are equal. As an example, the string `\"010\"` is alternating, while the string `\"0100\"` is not.\n\nOutput *the **smallest** number of operations needed to make* `s` *alternating*.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"0100\"\nOutput: 1\nExplanation: If you change the last character to '1', s will be \"0101\", which is alternating.\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"10\"\nOutput: 0\nExplanation: s is already alternating.\n```\n\n**Example 3:**\n\n```\nInput: s = \"1111\"\nOutput: 2\nExplanation: You need two operations to reach \"0101\" or \"1010\".\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `1 <= s.length <= 104`\n* `s[i]` is either `'0'` or `'1'`.",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
